text:
C1 is confirmed: local-time conversion can put visits in the wrong UTC day, a blocking correctness bug.

C2 is confirmed: the test checks only counts and misses incorrect date keys. Boundary timestamps and exact dictionary assertions should be added.

```json
{
  "verdicts": [
    {
      "id": "C1",
      "verdict": "confirmed",
      "reason": "visits_by_day promises UTC days but datetime.fromtimestamp(ts) uses the server's local timezone, which can assign visits to incorrect dates.",
      "evidence": ["app/visits.py:12", "app/visits.py:13"],
      "severity": "blocking"
    },
    {
      "id": "C2",
      "verdict": "confirmed",
      "reason": "The test uses noon timestamps and compares only counts, so incorrect date keys caused by local-time conversion still pass.",
      "evidence": ["tests/test_visits.py:9", "tests/test_visits.py:10", "tests/test_visits.py:11"],
      "severity": "should_fix"
    }
  ]
}
